      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "CH'ÊN Ta-shou 陳大受 (T. 占咸, H. 可齋), Aug. 15, 1702–1751, Oct. 9, official, was a native of Ch'i-yang, Hunan. In 1729 he took his chü-jên degree in Peking, and four years later became a chin-shih, with appointment as bachelor of the Hanlin Academy.",
